This product bundles brand marks from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org),
which are released under CC0 1.0 Universal:

    https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons/blob/develop/LICENSE.md

The icon artwork is bundled so that a diagram can name a brand and get its mark
without a network call. The marks themselves remain the trademarks of their
respective owners, and their inclusion here implies no affiliation with or
endorsement by those owners. Amazon, AWS, Azure and Oracle asked Simple Icons to
drop their marks, so those are not carried at all.

This product also bundles the Inter typeface (https://rsms.me/inter/), which is
released under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 — the licence text travels with it,
in assets/OFL.txt:

    https://github.com/rsms/inter

The font ships because a rasterizer that draws with whatever the machine happens
to have installed produces a different picture per machine, and the promise here
is the opposite: the same diagram, the same pixels, from the CLI, the editor and
the browser alike.

The rasterizer itself is resvg (https://github.com/linebender/resvg), used as the
WebAssembly build published as @resvg/resvg-wasm and licensed under the MPL 2.0.
It is a dependency rather than a copy, so its source and licence come with it.
